    "id": "fluid-boundary-layer-profile",
    "title": "Boundary-Layer Velocity Profile",
    "field": "Fluid Dynamics / Aerodynamics",
    "plotType": "Velocity profile (distance from wall vs. streamwise velocity)",
    "description": "A boundary-layer profile plots height above a surface against the streamwise flow velocity at that height, showing how flow speed climbs from zero at the wall (the no-slip condition) up to the free-stream value at the boundary-layer edge. The curvature of the profile encodes the flow regime: laminar layers rise gradually in a rounded curve, turbulent layers rise steeply near the wall then flatten. It is the foundational diagnostic for skin friction, heat transfer, and flow separation.",
