    "whatItTellsYou": "The point where a line from the origin is tangent to the curve gives the maximum lift-to-drag ratio, the most efficient operating condition. The leftmost point is the minimum drag. A curve shifted right means more drag for the same lift (a less efficient shape), and the bend at the top marks the onset of stall where drag rises sharply.",
